// Golden regression test that DISTINGUISHES a correct SRET-by-value compile
// from a move-codegen aliasing miscompile of the hazard `c = combine(c, g(c))`.
//
// V4 is a SMALL aggregate (4 i64) so today's copy-everywhere souc compiles and
// runs it WITHOUT stack overflow. The functions return V4 BY VALUE (SRET).
//
// Two hazard variants, to cover both inner-slot aliasing and arg-order
// sensitivity (the future arg-move wedge):
